[TEXT] All evidence confirms the fault. Here is the exact pattern:

| Traffic | Path | Result |
|---|---|---|
| cs_hod → 1.0.0.1 (server room) | must be forwarded through router1 | **100% loss** |
| cs_hod → 192.168.3.1 (router1's own LAN IP) | hits router1's INPUT chain | works |
| router1 → 1.0.0.1 (self-originated) | hits router1's OUTPUT chain | works |
| router1 → 192.168.1.1 (self-originated) | hits router1's OUTPUT chain | works |

The fault is definitively localized to router1's FORWARD chain.

